{"id":"dfc176599ab6a95f","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-klein-completeness.md","title":"Effective Enumerability of Theorems","display":"Effective Enumerability of Theorems","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-klein-completeness","aliases":["93-thm-klein-completeness"],"display":"Effective Enumerability of Theorems","depends_on":["[[93-df-recursive-enumerable]]","[[93-df-theorem]]","[[93-df-proof]]","[[93-df-set-theoretic-background]]","[[93-df-computable]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-klein-completeness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-klein-completeness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Effective Enumerability of Theorems"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5e8def090e751b3f\" href=\"?note=5e8def090e751b3f\" title=\"93-df-recursive-enumerable\">93-df-recursive-enumerable</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7a32f7aa28ab29ca\" href=\"?note=7a32f7aa28ab29ca\" title=\"93-df-theorem\">93-df-theorem</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"4e0a05ab276dc277\" href=\"?note=4e0a05ab276dc277\" title=\"93-df-proof\">93-df-proof</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e30eac382dc7d1a7\" href=\"?note=e30eac382dc7d1a7\" title=\"93-df-set-theoretic-background\">93-df-set-theoretic-background</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"172b7ec1d3eb81a8\" href=\"?note=172b7ec1d3eb81a8\" title=\"93-df-computable\">93-df-computable</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-klein-completeness-—-Effective-Enumerability-of-Theorems\">thm-klein-completeness — Effective Enumerability of Theorems</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> is a formula-set candidate and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P\">\\(\\mathcal P\\)</span> is a deductive-calculus candidate over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c_{\\mathsf{prf}}\">\\(c_{\\mathsf{prf}}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c_{\\mathsf{fml}}\">\\(c_{\\mathsf{fml}}\\)</span> are proposed injective codes of proof objects and formulas into <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}\">\\(\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}\">\\(\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}\">\\(\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}\\)</span> are defined here.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\ell_{\\mathcal P}:\\omega\\to\\omega\">\\(\\ell_{\\mathcal P}:\\omega\\to\\omega\\)</span> is a proposed computable last-formula map, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Computable}\">\\(\\mathrm{Computable}\\)</span> is the predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"172b7ec1d3eb81a8\" href=\"?note=172b7ec1d3eb81a8\" title=\"93-df-computable\">93-df-computable</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Thm}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Thm}_{93}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RE}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{RE}_{93}\\)</span> are sourced from the cited definitions.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\\in V\">\\(F\\in V\\)</span>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{prf}})\">\\(\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{prf}})\\)</span> 的编码参数满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c_{\\mathsf{prf}}:\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\to\\omega\">\\(c_{\\mathsf{prf}}:\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\to\\omega\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{fml}})\">\\(\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{fml}})\\)</span> 的编码参数满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c_{\\mathsf{fml}}:F\\to\\omega\">\\(c_{\\mathsf{fml}}:F\\to\\omega\\)</span>。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>以上是两个编码集合构造各自的取值域条件；单射性、可计算性、递归可枚举性及末公式相容性只按下方定理的显式前提使用。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\coloneqq\n\\{p:\\exists\\varphi\\in F\\;\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}(p,\\varphi,\\mathcal P)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\coloneqq\n\\{p:\\exists\\varphi\\in F\\;\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}(p,\\varphi,\\mathcal P)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{prf}})\\coloneqq\n\\{c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(p):p\\in\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{prf}})\\coloneqq\n\\{c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(p):p\\in\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{fml}})\\coloneqq\n\\{c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\varphi):\\varphi\\in F\\land\n\\mathrm{Thm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\mathcal P)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{fml}})\\coloneqq\n\\{c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\varphi):\\varphi\\in F\\land\n\\mathrm{Thm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\mathcal P)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\n\\land c_{\\mathsf{prf}}:\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\to\\omega\n\\land c_{\\mathsf{fml}}:F\\to\\omega\n\\land\\forall p,q\\in\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\;\n\\bigl(c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(p)=c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(q)\\to p=q\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall\\varphi,\\psi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl(c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\varphi)=c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\psi)\\to\\varphi=\\psi\\bigr)\n\\land\\ell_{\\mathcal P}:\\omega\\to\\omega\n\\land\\mathrm{Computable}(\\ell_{\\mathcal P})\n\\land\\forall p\\in\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}(p,\\varphi,\\mathcal P)\\to\n\\ell_{\\mathcal P}(c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(p))=c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\varphi)\\Bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{RE}_{93}\\bigl(\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{prf}})\\bigr)\n\\to\\mathrm{RE}_{93}\\bigl(\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{fml}})\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}klein\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\n\\land c_{\\mathsf{prf}}:\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\to\\omega\n\\land c_{\\mathsf{fml}}:F\\to\\omega\n\\land\\forall p,q\\in\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\;\n\\bigl(c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(p)=c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(q)\\to p=q\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall\\varphi,\\psi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl(c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\varphi)=c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\psi)\\to\\varphi=\\psi\\bigr)\n\\land\\ell_{\\mathcal P}:\\omega\\to\\omega\n\\land\\mathrm{Computable}(\\ell_{\\mathcal P})\n\\land\\forall p\\in\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}(p,\\varphi,\\mathcal P)\\to\n\\ell_{\\mathcal P}(c_{\\mathsf{prf}}(p))=c_{\\mathsf{fml}}(\\varphi)\\Bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{RE}_{93}\\bigl(\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{prf}})\\bigr)\n\\to\\mathrm{RE}_{93}\\bigl(\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}(\\mathcal P,F;c_{\\mathsf{fml}})\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The compatibility clause makes the image of the proof-code set under <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\ell_{\\mathcal P}\">\\(\\ell_{\\mathcal P}\\)</span> exactly the displayed theorem-code set: every proof ends in a theorem, and every theorem has a proof by definition. Thus the conclusion is closure of recursively enumerable subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span> under computable images. The coding maps, their domains, and injectivity are now object-language data rather than prose notation. No converse is asserted. The legacy filename is retained.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-klein-completeness-—-Effective-Enumerability-of-Theorems","text":"thm-klein-completeness — Effective Enumerability of Theorems","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-recursive-enumerable","status":"resolved","id":"5e8def090e751b3f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-recursive-enumerable]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-theorem","status":"resolved","id":"7a32f7aa28ab29ca","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-theorem]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-proof","status":"resolved","id":"4e0a05ab276dc277","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-proof]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-set-theoretic-background","status":"resolved","id":"e30eac382dc7d1a7","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-set-theoretic-background]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-computable","status":"resolved","id":"172b7ec1d3eb81a8","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-computable]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-computable","status":"resolved","id":"172b7ec1d3eb81a8","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\ell_{\\mathcal P}:\\omega\\to\\omega$ is a proposed computable last-formula map, and $\\mathrm{Computable}$ is the predicate of [[93-df-computable]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal P","display":false},{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"c_{\\mathsf{prf}}","display":false},{"tex":"c_{\\mathsf{fml}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PrfObj}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PrfCode}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ThmCode}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\ell_{\\mathcal P}:\\omega\\to\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Computable}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Thm}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RE}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"F\\in V","display":false},{"tex"